Well, the onslaught mode DOES have the merit of focusing the combat in 
particular areas of the map - you don't have to wander around endlessly 
to find somebody to fight, and you're more or less guaranteed (if your 
teammates have half a brain) to have backup in combat. At the same time, 
it allows you SOME latitude for sneakiness - most maps AFAICS have some 
"alternate route" to the enemy, and even if they don't, it's possible to 
camp outside the enemy's gate and whittle down their forces (in effect, 
striking at their supply lines) so your front-line people can cover 
ground more easily.

It's sort of like rugby (the "scrums" over control points), only with 
very large guns and other assorted hardware...

